# Day 47

## Experiment Title

Introduction to Jenkins and Continuous Integration


## Objective

To understand the basics of Jenkins and study its role in Continuous Integration and automation.


## Theory

Jenkins is an open source automation server used for Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment. It helps developers automate tasks such as application building, testing, and deployment.

Jenkins supports plugins and pipelines that simplify software development workflows. It improves development efficiency by automatically executing tasks whenever code changes occur in the project repository.


## Requirements

Jenkins

Java Development Kit

Docker Desktop

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Install Jenkins on the system or run Jenkins using Docker.

Open the Jenkins dashboard through the web browser.

Study the Jenkins user interface and available options.

Understand the role of Jenkins in Continuous Integration.

Observe Jenkins services and system configuration.


## Output

Jenkins was installed and configured successfully.

The Jenkins dashboard was accessed successfully through the browser.

Continuous Integration concepts using Jenkins were studied successfully.


## Result

Successfully understood the basics of Jenkins and Continuous Integration.
